# Workboard

Requires Node.js 22.22.1. Uses built-in HTTP and SQLite with no external dependencies.

Start the application:

```sh
PORT=8080 DB_PATH=./data/workboard.sqlite npm start
```

Open `http://localhost:8080`. Both variables are optional and default to the values above. The server binds to `0.0.0.0`. SQLite stores projects, tasks, completion state, and archive state across restarts. Existing databases migrate automatically. Open a project to create tasks, toggle completion, or filter by All, Open, Completed, and Deleted. Use the Project filter to view Active or Archived projects. Archive or restore a project from its row; archived project tasks remain readable and filterable, with editing disabled. Each row shows completed and total task counts. `GET /health` returns `{"status":"ok"}`.

Run the integration checks:

```sh
npm test
```

On an active project page, enter a New project name and select Rename project. Names are trimmed and saved without changing the project URL, creation order, tasks, or completion counts. Blank names show an alert. Archived projects cannot be renamed until restored.

Each task row provides New task title and Rename task controls. Task titles are trimmed and saved while preserving ownership, creation order, completion state, filter membership, and completion counts. Blank titles show an alert. Archived projects disable task renaming until restored.

Each task row also has a Task priority selector with Low, Normal, and High options. Existing tasks default to Normal during migration. Priority changes save independently without changing task order, completion, or summaries; renaming preserves priority. Archived projects disable priority editing until restored. Priorities persist across reloads and server restarts.

Each project has a Default task priority selector with Low, Normal, and High options, initially Normal. New tasks inherit the project's saved default. Changing it preserves existing tasks and both task filter selections. Defaults are independent per project and persist through renaming, restarts, archival, and restoration. Archived projects display the saved default with editing disabled.

Each task has a Task due date textbox and Save due date button. Dates are optional; blank input clears them. Nonempty input is trimmed and must be a real Gregorian date in YYYY-MM-DD format, with a year from 0001 through 9999. Invalid dates show an alert and leave the saved date unchanged. Dates persist without timezone conversion, independently of other task data and both filter selections. Archived projects disable due-date editing until restored.

Each project page provides Due from and Due through textboxes and Apply due range. Boundaries are inclusive, optional, trimmed, and validated using the same calendar rules as task due dates. Any nonblank boundary excludes undated tasks. The applied range intersects completion and priority filters, retains their selections, and remains applied through edits and validation errors. Invalid or reversed ranges show an alert and preserve the previous membership. Range controls remain usable when archived. Opening a project from the list resets all task filters and range boundaries. Filtering never changes saved tasks or all-task completion summaries.

Each task row has a Destination project selector and Move task button. Destinations are active projects other than the current project, listed by project creation order using their current names. A first-time move appends the task after all positions already established in the destination. Returning to a previous project restores its remembered position relative to other tasks, even when multiple tasks return in a different order. Each project's position history persists independently, while the task keeps its current ID, title, completion, priority, and due date. The source stays open with its filters and due range retained; both projects' summaries reflect their current tasks. Archived projects cannot send or receive tasks. Moving is disabled when no eligible destination exists. Saved task order migrates automatically and persists through repeated moves and restarts.

Tests start isolated server processes and remove their temporary database directories after checking validation, creation order, navigation, task filters, project isolation, restart persistence, database migration, archive/restore, editing protection, completion summaries, renaming, and moves with preserved task data, first-time append order, and remembered return positions across projects and restarts.

Project search and Search projects match a trimmed substring of project names, ignoring ASCII letter case and treating runs of spaces and tabs as a single space. Search intersects the Active/Archived filter, and changing that filter retains the applied query. Opening the list or returning via Projects starts with an empty query.

Task search and Search tasks use the same matching rules and intersect completion, priority, and applied due-range filters. Search, filter changes, task edits, creation, movement, project renaming, and default-priority changes retain the other applied view settings and re-evaluate matching rows without changing saved task data or summaries. Task search remains usable in archived projects. Opening a project from the list resets its search. Integration checks cover search matching, filter intersections, edit retention, archive restrictions, saved data, and remembered movement order across restart.

Each task row has a multiline Task notes textarea and Save notes button. Notes save as plain text without trimming, preserving spaces, line breaks, Unicode, and literal markup. Empty text clears them. Existing databases initialize only the new notes field to empty. Notes persist across reloads and restarts and travel with tasks through moves and remembered return positions. Saving notes retains all applied filters and search settings; searches still match only project names or task titles. Archived projects show saved notes with both notes controls disabled until restoration.

Live task rows provide Delete task; the Deleted task filter shows saved deleted tasks with Restore task. Deleted tasks are excluded from live filters and completion summaries. Deletion retains every saved field and remembered project position, and restoration returns the task to its reserved position. All other deleted-task controls are disabled, and archived projects also disable deletion and restoration. The Deleted filter intersects priority, due range, and title search. Deletion and restoration retain the applied view and persist through restarts; existing tasks migrate as live.

Every project page provides Download project, including archived and empty projects. It downloads UTF-8 `workboard-project.json` with format `workboard-project`, version 1, and the project's current name, archive state, default priority, and all live and deleted tasks in stored order. Task fields include title, completion, explicit priority, due date, notes, and deletion state. Notes line endings are represented as LF in the export; stored notes remain unchanged. Downloading ignores page filters and searches and preserves all saved data, remembered task positions, and the current view.

The home page provides Project JSON, Imported project name, and Import project. Import validates every required version 1 field and Gregorian date before writing anything, then creates a separate project and tasks in one transaction and opens it. The trimmed override name is required; rejected imports show an alert, retain both submitted fields, and leave all saved data unchanged. Imported titles remain exact, notes use LF line endings, and archive/deletion states, priorities, dates, completion, and task order persist independently of the original project. Extra properties cannot supply internal IDs or positions. Imported tasks participate in the existing move/return-position rules.
import { createServer } from 'node:http';
import { DatabaseSync } from 'node:sqlite';
import { mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';
import { dirname } from 'node:path';

const port = Number(process.env.PORT ?? 8080);
const dbPath = process.env.DB_PATH ?? 'data/workboard.sqlite';
mkdirSync(dirname(dbPath), { recursive: true });
const db = new DatabaseSync(dbPath);
db.exec('PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON');
db.exec(`
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS projects (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    name TEXT NOT NULL
  );
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tasks (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    project_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES projects(id),
    title TEXT NOT NULL,
    completed INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (completed IN (0, 1))
  )
`);
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(projects)').all().some(column => column.name === 'archived')) {
  db.exec('ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN archived INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (archived IN (0, 1))');
}
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(tasks)').all().some(column => column.name === 'priority')) {
  db.exec("ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN priority TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Normal' CHECK (priority IN ('Low', 'Normal', 'High'))");
}
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(projects)').all().some(column => column.name === 'default_priority')) {
  db.exec("ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN default_priority TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Normal' CHECK (default_priority IN ('Low', 'Normal', 'High'))");
}
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(tasks)').all().some(column => column.name === 'due_date')) {
  db.exec("ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN due_date TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''");
}
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(tasks)').all().some(column => column.name === 'notes')) {
  db.exec("ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN notes TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''");
}
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(tasks)').all().some(column => column.name === 'deleted')) {
  db.exec('ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN deleted INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (deleted IN (0, 1))');
}
if (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(tasks)').all().some(column => column.name === 'position')) {
  db.exec('BEGIN');
  try {
    db.exec('ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN position INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0');
    db.exec('UPDATE tasks SET position = id');
    db.exec('COMMIT');
  } catch (error) {
    db.exec('ROLLBACK');
    throw error;
  }
}
db.exec(`
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS task_positions (
    task_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES tasks(id),
    project_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES projects(id),
    position INTEGER NOT NULL,
    PRIMARY KEY (task_id, project_id)
  );
  CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS task_positions_project_order ON task_positions(project_id, position);
  INSERT OR IGNORE INTO task_positions (task_id, project_id, position)
    SELECT id, project_id, position FROM tasks;
`);
const taskPriorities = ['Low', 'Normal', 'High'];
const taskFilters = ['All', 'Open', 'Completed', 'Deleted'];
const listProjects = db.prepare(`
  SELECT projects.id, projects.name, projects.archived,
    COUNT(tasks.id) AS total_count, COALESCE(SUM(tasks.completed), 0) AS completed_count
  FROM projects LEFT JOIN tasks ON tasks.project_id = projects.id AND tasks.deleted = 0
  WHERE projects.archived = ? GROUP BY projects.id ORDER BY projects.id
`);
const findProject = db.prepare('SELECT id, name, archived, default_priority FROM projects WHERE id = ?');
const setDefaultPriority = db.prepare('UPDATE projects SET default_priority = ? WHERE id = ?');
const setArchived = db.prepare('UPDATE projects SET archived = ? WHERE id = ?');
const renameProject = db.prepare('UPDATE projects SET name = ? WHERE id = ?');
const addProject = db.prepare('INSERT INTO projects (name) VALUES (?)');
const addImportedProject = db.prepare('INSERT INTO projects (name, archived, default_priority) VALUES (?, ?, ?)');
const addImportedTask = db.prepare(`
  INSERT INTO tasks (project_id, title, completed, priority, due_date, notes, deleted, position)
  VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)
`);
const listDestinations = db.prepare('SELECT id, name FROM projects WHERE archived = 0 AND id != ? ORDER BY id');
const listTasks = db.prepare('SELECT id, title, completed, priority, due_date, notes, deleted FROM tasks WHERE project_id = ? ORDER BY position, id');
const addTask = db.prepare(`
  INSERT INTO tasks (project_id, title, priority, position)
  VALUES (?, ?, ?, (SELECT COALESCE(MAX(position), 0) + 1 FROM task_positions WHERE project_id = ?))
`);
const rememberCreatedTask = db.prepare(`
  INSERT INTO task_positions (task_id, project_id, position)
  SELECT id, project_id, position FROM tasks WHERE id = ?
`);
const rememberDestination = db.prepare(`
  INSERT OR IGNORE INTO task_positions (task_id, project_id, position)
  SELECT id, ?, (SELECT COALESCE(MAX(position), 0) + 1 FROM task_positions WHERE project_id = ?)
  FROM tasks WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?
`);
const moveTask = db.prepare(`
  UPDATE tasks SET project_id = ?,
    position = (SELECT position FROM task_positions WHERE project_id = ? AND task_id = ?)
  WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?
`);
const updateTask = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET completed = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const renameTask = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET title = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const setTaskPriority = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET priority = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const setTaskDueDate = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET due_date = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const findTask = db.prepare('SELECT deleted FROM tasks WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const setTaskDeleted = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET deleted = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');
const setTaskNotes = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET notes = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');

function transaction(action) {
  db.exec('BEGIN');
  try {
    const result = action();
    db.exec('COMMIT');
    return result;
  } catch (error) {
    db.exec('ROLLBACK');
    throw error;
  }
}

function validDueDate(value) {
  if (value === '') return true;
  if (!/^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$/.test(value)) return false;
  const [year, month, day] = value.split('-').map(Number);
  if (year < 1 || month < 1 || month > 12 || day < 1) return false;
  const leapYear = year % 4 === 0 && (year % 100 !== 0 || year % 400 === 0);
  const daysInMonth = [31, leapYear ? 29 : 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31];
  return day <= daysInMonth[month - 1];
}

function parseProjectImport(json) {
  let document;
  try {
    document = JSON.parse(json);
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
  const object = value => value !== null && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value);
  const nonblank = value => typeof value === 'string' && value.trim() !== '';
  if (!object(document) || document.format !== 'workboard-project' || document.version !== 1) return null;
  const project = document.project;
  if (!object(project) || !nonblank(project.name) || typeof project.archived !== 'boolean' ||
      !taskPriorities.includes(project.defaultPriority) || !Array.isArray(project.tasks)) return null;
  for (const task of project.tasks) {
    if (!object(task) || !nonblank(task.title) || typeof task.completed !== 'boolean' ||
        !taskPriorities.includes(task.priority) || typeof task.dueDate !== 'string' ||
        !validDueDate(task.dueDate) || typeof task.notes !== 'string' ||
        typeof task.deleted !== 'boolean') return null;
  }
  return project;
}

function importProject(project, name) {
  return transaction(() => {
    const projectId = addImportedProject.run(name, Number(project.archived), project.defaultPriority).lastInsertRowid;
    project.tasks.forEach((task, index) => {
      const taskId = addImportedTask.run(projectId, task.title, Number(task.completed), task.priority,
        task.dueDate, task.notes.replace(/\r\n?/g, '\n'), Number(task.deleted), index + 1).lastInsertRowid;
      rememberCreatedTask.run(taskId);
    });
    return projectId;
  });
}

function taskFilter(value) {
  return taskFilters.includes(value) ? value : 'All';
}

function priorityFilter(value) {
  return taskPriorities.includes(value) ? value : 'All';
}

function dueRange(values, fromKey = 'dueFrom', throughKey = 'dueThrough') {
  const from = (values.get(fromKey) ?? '').trim();
  const through = (values.get(throughKey) ?? '').trim();
  return validDueDate(from) && validDueDate(through) && (!from || !through || from <= through)
    ? { from, through } : { from: '', through: '' };
}

function searchQuery(values, key) {
  return (values.get(key) ?? '').trim();
}

function matchesSearch(value, query) {
  const normalize = text => text.replace(/[ \t]+/g, ' ')
    .replace(/[A-Z]/g, letter => letter.toLowerCase());
  return normalize(value).includes(normalize(query));
}

function searchField(key, query) {
  return `<input type="hidden" name="${key}" value="${escapeHtml(query)}">`;
}

function rangeFields(range, query = '') {
  return `${searchField('taskSearch', query)}<input type="hidden" name="dueFrom" value="${escapeHtml(range.from)}">
    <input type="hidden" name="dueThrough" value="${escapeHtml(range.through)}">`;
}

function projectPath(projectId, filter, priority, range = { from: '', through: '' }, query = '') {
  const params = new URLSearchParams();
  if (filter !== 'All') params.set('filter', filter);
  if (priority !== 'All') params.set('priorityFilter', priority);
  if (range.from) params.set('dueFrom', range.from);
  if (range.through) params.set('dueThrough', range.through);
  if (query) params.set('taskSearch', query);
  return `/projects/${projectId}${params.size ? `?${params}` : ''}`;
}

function escapeHtml(value) {
  return String(value).replace(/[&<>"']/g, character => ({
    '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;', "'": '&#39;',
  })[character]);
}

function page(title, content) {
  return `<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>${escapeHtml(title)} · Workboard</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
</head>
<body><main>${content}</main></body>
</html>`;
}

